<%# locals: (thumb:, ext_label:, url:, photo: false) %>
<%#
  Shared thumbnail box for a renderable file, used by both the list and grid views. The poll
  controller (thumbs_controller.js) finds `.thumb` inside a `.file-cell` and swaps the spinner for
  the <img> once ready, or a static badge on unsupported/failed. Sizing comes from the ancestor
  container (table.files .thumb vs .files-grid .thumb), so this markup is size-agnostic.

  Locals: `thumb` (a Maker::Preview or nil), `ext_label` (String), `url` (String or nil), `photo`
  (Boolean, default false).

  `photo` CROPS A CAMERA FORMAT TO FILL ITS STAGE (`.thumb.photo`, Maker::FileAttachment.photo?;
  structural redesign slice 3). It defaults to FALSE so every caller that does not ask — the public
  surfaces among them — renders exactly as before. The class sits on the span, which the poll
  never replaces (thumbs_controller swaps its children only), so it survives the render landing.

  `url` IS A STRICT LOCAL BECAUSE THIS PARTIAL IS SHARED BY A SESSION-AUTHED PAGE AND A SESSIONLESS
  ONE (hardening, 2026-09-08; tinkerex#278) — the same design the eight viewer partials already use
  for every URL they need. The maker's pages pass `preview_src(thumb)` (`url_for(asset)`, unchanged
  behaviour); a visitor's pass `pub.preview_url_for(node_id)`, which goes through the project's own
  permission and expires. Building the URL here instead is what made a public cover keep answering
  after its project went private, so `url_for` is refused in this file by the Public seam guard's
  third arm (test/architecture_invariants_test.rb) — pass it in, never derive it.
%>
<span class="thumb<%= " photo" if photo %>" data-thumbs-target="thumb">
  <% if thumb&.status == "ready" && thumb.asset.attached? %>
    <img src="<%= url %>" alt="" loading="lazy">
  <% elsif thumb.nil? || %w[pending processing].include?(thumb&.status) %>
    <span class="thumb-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <% else %>
    <%# THE TERMINAL STATE: unsupported, failed, or no row at all. It SAYS SO rather than showing a
        bare badge — a cover card passes `ext_label: ""`, so this rendered an empty box that read
        as "still loading" next to a real spinner. `title` is what a hover reveals; the badge text
        stays the extension where there is one, because that is the more useful glance. Not
        aria-hidden any more: the label is the only thing telling a screen reader this file has no
        preview, and hiding it left nothing at all. %>
    <span class="thumb-icon" title="Preview not supported"><%= ext_label.presence || "—" %></span>
  <% end %>
</span>
